quran[31]{c,v,t}:
  79,16,"When his Lord called out to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa,"
  79,17,"(commanding:) ‘Go to Pharaoh, for indeed he has rebelled,"
  79,18,and say (to him): ‘Would you like to purify yourself?
  79,19,I will guide you to your Lord so that you may fear (Him).’’
  79,20,Then he showed him the most significant sign.
  79,21,But he denied and disobeyed.
  79,22,"Then he turned back, swiftly endeavouring (in his scheme against Musa [Moses])."
  79,23,"So he gathered (his people) and called out,"
  79,24,"saying: ‘I am your lord, the most exalted!’"
  79,25,So Allah overtook him with an exemplary punishment in the Hereafter and this world.
  79,26,"Surely, in this (incident), there is an admonition for one who fears (Allah)."
  79,27,Are you more difficult to create or (the entire) universe that He has built?
  79,28,"He raised all its heavenly spheres (by expanding them from all sides), then fashioned them perfectly."
  79,29,Then darkened its night and brought out its daylight.
  79,30,"As for the earth, He separated (it from the solar nebula) and expanded it after that (to make it inhabitable)."
  79,31,He brought out its water from it (separately) and its green pastures (from the rest of the dry regions).
  79,32,"As for the mountains, He raised them firmly (upon it)."
  79,33,(He did all this) as a (means of) sustenance for you and your livestock.
  79,34,"When the great overwhelming catastrophe arrives,"
  79,35,"that Day, every human being will remember whatever he has endeavoured."
  79,36,The Hellfire will be made visible to all who can see.
  79,37,"As for him, who was rebellious,"
  79,38,"and preferred the life of this world,"
  79,39,the Hellfire will certainly be (his) refuge.
  79,40,"But as for those who feared standing in the presence of his Lord and restrained (his) soul from evil desires,"
  79,41,"indeed, Paradise will be his abode."
  79,42,They (the disbelievers) ask you about the Hour: ‘When shall it set in?’
  79,43,What do you have to do with mentioning it?
  79,44,(Tell them that) towards your Lord is its conclusion.
  79,45,You are only a Warner for one who fears it.
  79,46,"On the Day they see it, it shall be as if they had stayed (in the world) no more than an evening or forenoon."
